        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Architecture California - September/October 1983</title>\n  <script>\n    window.MathJax = { tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$']] } };\n  </script>\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      background: #eee;\n      color: #111;\n      font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    }\n    .page {\n      width: 1000px;\n      min-height: 1420px;\n      margin: 10px auto;\n      padding: 55px 43px 40px;\n      background: #fffefa;\n      border: 1px solid #bdbdb4;\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 64.3% 35.7%;\n    }\n    .left {\n      padding-right: 8px;\n      border-right: 1px solid #111;\n    }\n    .right {\n      padding: 52px 28px 0 12px;\n    }\n    .book-ad {\n      position: relative;\n      height: 588px;\n      padding: 37px 25px;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      color: white;\n      background: #272727;\n    }\n    .book-ad h1 {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 40px;\n      line-height: 1.36;\n      font-weight: normal;\n      letter-spacing: 1px;\n    }\n    .book-copy {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 26px;\n      top: 230px;\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 20px;\n      line-height: 1.18;\n      font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    .building {\n      position: absolute;\n      right: 4px;\n      bottom: 9px;\n      width: 390px;\n      height: 420px;\n      color: #111;\n      background:\n        repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 0 8px, rgba(15,15,15,.45) 9px 10px),\n        repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 0 8px, rgba(15,15,15,.45) 9px 10px),\n        #f8f8f3;\n      clip-path: polygon(47% 0, 61% 13%, 73% 5%, 88% 23%, 82% 51%, 100% 66%, 87% 81%, 74% 71%, 66% 100%, 49% 84%, 31% 91%, 22% 68%, 0 59%, 10% 38%, 29% 42%, 36% 18%);\n      border: 2px solid #111;\n    }\n    .book-brand {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 22px;\n      bottom: 91px;\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 37px;\n      line-height: .88;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      letter-spacing: 1px;\n    }\n    .book-brand small {\n      display: block;\n      margin-top: 26px;\n      font-size: 19px;\n      line-height: 1.1;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-weight: normal;\n    }\n    .vertical-credit {\n      position: absolute;\n      right: -18px;\n      top: 150px;\n      height: 310px;\n      writing-mode: vertical-rl;\n      transform: rotate(180deg);\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 11px;\n      letter-spacing: .4px;\n      color: #111;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    .furniture-ad {\n      position: relative;\n      height: 596px;\n      margin-top: 13px;\n      border: 1px solid #111;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      background: #fff;\n    }\n    .furniture-ad h2 {\n      margin: 9px 13px 0;\n      font-size: 42px;\n      line-height: 1;\n      letter-spacing: -2px;\n    }\n    .furniture-title {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 61px;\n      left: 13px;\n      font-size: 40px;\n      line-height: .78;\n      letter-spacing: -3px;\n      color: #fff;\n      text-shadow:\n        -1px -1px 0 #111, 1px -1px 0 #111,\n        -1px 1px 0 #111, 1px 1px 0 #111;\n    }\n    .furniture-title sup {\n      font-size: 12px;\n      letter-spacing: 0;\n      vertical-align: top;\n    }\n    .furniture-copy {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 169px;\n      left: 14px;\n      width: 150px;\n      font-size: 11px;\n      line-height: 1.12;\n      font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    .furniture-copy p { margin: 0 0 8px; }\n    .chair {\n      position: absolute;\n      right: 8px;\n      bottom: 15px;\n      width: 405px;\n      height: 435px;\n      background: #fff;\n    }\n    .chair .back {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 5px;\n      left: 148px;\n      width: 170px;\n      height: 128px;\n      background: repeating-linear-gradient(165deg, #999 0 5px, #333 6px 10px, #ddd 11px 15px);\n      border: 11px solid #111;\n      border-radius: 16px 22px 2px 2px;\n      transform: skewY(-17deg);\n    }\n    .chair .seat {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 180px;\n      left: 27px;\n      width: 275px;\n      height: 135px;\n      border: 15px solid #111;\n      border-radius: 13px;\n      background: repeating-linear-gradient(140deg, #aaa 0 8px, #333 9px 13px, #ddd 14px 21px);\n      transform: skewY(-11deg);\n    }\n    .chair .arm {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 10px;\n      top: 135px;\n      width: 105px;\n      height: 46px;\n      background: #111;\n      border-radius: 13px;\n      transform: rotate(10deg);\n    }\n    .chair .front {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 15px;\n      bottom: 0;\n      width: 183px;\n      height: 138px;\n      border: 18px solid #111;\n      border-bottom-width: 25px;\n      border-radius: 13px 13px 0 0;\n      background: white;\n    }\n    .timber {\n      height: 63px;\n      border: 1px solid #111;\n      border-top: 0;\n      padding: 12px 14px;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      gap: 27px;\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .timber strong {\n      font-size: 25px;\n      letter-spacing: -2px;\n    }\n    .timber div {\n      font-weight: bold;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      line-height: 1.05;\n    }\n    .small-top {\n      margin: 0 0 22px;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.16;\n    }\n    article { margin-bottom: 20px; }\n    article h2 {\n      margin: 0 0 4px;\n      font-size: 20px;\n      line-height: .95;\n    }\n    article p {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: .98;\n      text-indent: 15px;\n    }\n    ul {\n      margin: 1px 0 20px 13px;\n      padding-left: 15px;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: .98;\n    }\n    li { padding-left: 0; }\n    .footer {\n      margin-top: 18px;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      letter-spacing: .1px;\n    }\n    .footer b { margin-right: 12px; }\n    @media (max-width: 1040px) {\n      .page { width: 100%; margin: 0; }\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 700px) {\n      .page { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 25px 18px; }\n      .left { border-right: 0; padding-right: 0; }\n      .right { padding: 28px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid #111; }\n      .book-ad { transform-origin: top left; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <section class=\"left\">\n      <div class=\"book-ad\">\n        <h1>BOOKS ON<br>ARCHITECTURE</h1>\n        <div class=\"book-copy\">Send a business<br>card for a<br>Free catalog!</div>\n        <div class=\"building placeholder\" aria-label=\"Illustration of modern architectural buildings\">[Illustration: architectural building complex]</div>\n        <div class=\"book-brand\">builders<br>booksource\n          <small>1801 4th Street, Berkeley<br>(415) 845-6874</small>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"vertical-credit\">ILLUSTRATION FROM: HOUSE X&nbsp;&nbsp; PETER EISENMAN&nbsp;&nbsp; RIZZOLI INTERNATIONAL</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"furniture-ad\">\n        <h2>Improve your client's site.</h2>\n        <div class=\"furniture-title\">Civic<br>Furniture<sup>TM</sup></div>\n        <div class=\"furniture-copy\">\n          <p>This rugged family of contemporary Civic Furniture™ from TimberForm® may go a long way toward improving your client's site and making you look better too. Heavy cast iron bench ends combined with premium, thoroughly seasoned, hand selected hardwood, make these knockout site complements tough competitors and strong survivors in the hostile urban jungle.</p>\n          <p>Matching seats, benches, and litter containers are available in this and several other styles. Over 300 site complements appear in our latest catalog of Civic Furniture,™ mall amenities, and park and landscape accessories. For your personal copy, call <b>Toll-free 800/547-1940.</b></p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"chair placeholder\" aria-label=\"Photograph of civic furniture bench and chair\">\n          <div class=\"back\"></div>\n          <div class=\"seat\"></div>\n          <div class=\"arm\"></div>\n          <div class=\"front\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"timber\">\n        <strong>TIMBERFORM<sup>®</sup></strong>\n        <div>Columbia Cascade Timber Company<br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">1975 S.W. Fifth Avenue, Portland, Oregon 97201 U.S.A.</span></div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"footer\"><b>12</b> Architecture California&nbsp;&nbsp; September/October 1983</div>\n    </section>\n\n    <aside class=\"right\">\n      <p class=\"small-top\">CLCA, at Fiske Landscaping, #3 Cherry Hills Court, San Ramon, CA 94583, (415) 828-8680.</p>\n\n      <article>\n        <h2>Solar Tax Credits Lowered</h2>\n        <p>Legislation accompanying the State Budget made the following changes in California's solar, wind, and conservation tax credits, effective August 1, 1983:</p>\n        <ul>\n          <li>All tax credits for solar heating of pools and spas are eliminated.</li>\n          <li>The 55 percent solar tax credit is reduced to 50 percent.</li>\n          <li>The 40 percent conservation tax credit is reduced to 35 percent.</li>\n          <li>For solar, wind and conservation measures installed between August 1 and December 31, 1983, only one-half of available credits may be claimed against taxes for 1983, and the remainder claimed against future tax years.</li>\n          <li>Solar and wind energy tax credits are extended through 1986.</li>\n          <li>Conservation tax credits are extended through 1985.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n\n      <article>\n        <h2>Abolishing Historical Review<br>Board Causes Civic Controversy</h2>\n        <p>A move by the Fremont City Council to abolish the Historical Architectural Review Board (HARB) is meeting with stiff opposition from community groups, who have succeeded in placing a referendum on the November ballot which will allow local citizens to decide HARB's fate.</p>\n        <p>For 24 years, HARB has reviewed new projects and exterior modifications to existing buildings in the historic districts of Niles and Mission San Jose. HARB meets monthly, and is required by its enabling ordinance to complete its project review within 30 days of the project's submittal, according to city planner Fred Broumand, who also is HARB secretary. HARB's members, appointed by the City Council, include an architect, a landscape architect and three public members. If HARB is disbanded, its duties will be transferred to the city planning staff. Unlike HARB, the city planning staff does not sit as a public body.</p>\n        <p>Eliminating HARB is explained as an effort to reduce regulation. HARB “is just another level of government,” according to Mayor Leon Mezzetti, who told the Fremont <i>Argus</i> that HARB supporters are “a handful of self-appointed architects and historians in the Mission area that want to control the Mission” Groups advocating the retention of HARB include the Mission San Jose Chamber of Commerce, Niles Merchants Association, Mission Peak Heritage Foundation and the Committee for the Restoration of San Jose.</p>\n      </article>\n    </aside>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
